  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "For a **T'AU EMPIRE** [Army Faction](vsdata:core-rule/select-army-faction), when your [Shooting phase](vsdata:core-rule/shooting-phase) begins you may designate Observers from your own units. For each eligible **Observer**, mark one enemy it can see as **Spotted** through phase end. The **Observer** must be eligible to shoot and await selection for shooting. [Battle-shocked](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock) units and **FORTIFICATION** cannot mark an enemy. Each enemy can be marked only once that phase. When your non-Observer units target a **Spotted** enemy, they count as **Guided** against it. Improve their models’ attacking weapons’ Ballistic Skill by 1. The weapons also gain **[[IGNORES COVER]](vsdata:weapon-ability/ignores-cover)** for those attacks if the **Observer** that marked the enemy has **MARKERLIGHT**.",
